// src/v4/compiler/04_infer.dag
//
// Scope: pipeline stage 4 — type inference + checking. Single-file discipline; split = stop signal.
// Anchor: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Type_inference (Hindley–Milner family + algebra-homomorphism search per THESIS:173)
// Primary: this file (+ lens/* + std/algebra.dag grounding) is the
//   compiler's LOAD-BEARING work — validating the epistemic chain. Per
//   THESIS:13 + :196: the compiler is a causal/algebra engine first;
//   emission is mechanical translation downstream. Algebra-homomorphism
//   search here IS the enforcement; an ungroundable concept is a
//   Diagnostic, never a downstream emitter special-case.
//
// IR-1 (operator-ratified 2026-05-15) — the InferredTree contract,
// FROZEN now (not emergent — "this time we model the IR up front"):
//
//   InferredTree is NOT a new type. Per A1 it is the SAME `Node` tree
//   with one extra FLAT per-node coordinate populated — `InferredFacts`
//   — exactly as connective/behavior are flat coordinates. Modeling a
//   separate recursive `InferredNode` is THE bounded-kernel violation
//   that split v2 infer into 12 files = STOP, not a worker choice.
//
//   InferredFacts (flat, per-node; the FROZEN payload — a 5th field is a
//   substrate-extension STOP→escalate, never an inline add):
//     - resolved_type : Node          (the node's type — itself a Node in
//                                       the type substrate, Shape S)
//     - inhabits      : AlgebraRef    (which algebra — the U1 homomorphism
//                                       carrier; grounds cost AND codegen)
//     - cost          : SymbolicCost  (the U1 carrier; termination ∧
//                                       complexity are ONE datum — A2/U2,
//                                       consumed from cost.dag, not re-derived)
//     - descent       : DescentEvidence  (A2: Implicit(sub-Node descent —
//                                       free, no carrier) | Explicit(
//                                       RankingDimensionRef → T-3 cardinality.dag))
//   - NOT fields (single-authority, P2 — they are already carried by
//     `resolved_type`'s Node structure; caching = a second authority):
//       * cardinality — the Cardinality connective IS one of the 6 (A1);
//         it is read from `resolved_type`, never stored (correction
//         3248488135).
//       * effects — per B3 the type signature is the single effect
//         authority; read from `resolved_type`, never stored.
//
// C1 (operator-ratified 2026-05-15) — infer is the bounded *Find* phase
//   of the one U1 homomorphism. The algebra-homomorphism search is
//   BOUNDED STRUCTURAL UNIFICATION over the finite (by A1/A2) candidate
//   space — never an open search. An empty result is a helpful
//   Diagnostic (feedback_no_engine), NEVER a fabricated coercion. The v2
//   12-file split cannot recur (its cause — a separate recursive inferred
//   type — is structurally gone via IR-1/A1).
//
// B-4 (side-session 2026-05-15; carrier corrected per a P2/Practice-3
//   review finding on PR #3162) — the affected_set R2 minimality
//   contract. NAMED CARRIER, not resolved_type:
//   - The use→def fact's forward carrier is the post-resolution opaque
//     `Symbol` (K-1) on the name-reference `Atom` — NOT `resolved_type`.
//     `resolved_type` is the node's *type*; many declarations share a
//     type, so it is LOSSY for binding identity (the review's point —
//     citing it was a Practice-3/P2 error). The correct carrier already
//     exists and is named: the `Symbol`.
//   - AUTHORITY is compiler/03_resolve.dag (it owns "identifier binding
//     to declarations"). Resolution canonicalizes a use-site `Atom`'s
//     `Symbol` to be IDENTICAL to its binder declaration's `Symbol`, so
//     binding = `Symbol` equality (the one K-1-granted op; node.dag's
//     `name_occurrences` pattern; "resolved through the namespace" per
//     A1/K-1). That canonical `Symbol` rides in `ResolvedTree`.
//   - 04_infer's obligation here is PRESERVE-ONLY: infer adds
//     `InferredFacts`; it MUST NOT alter or drop the resolved `Symbol`
//     identity. infer neither owns nor re-carries the use→def fact (so
//     no 5th `InferredFacts` field — IR-1-safe; the fact's authority is
//     03_resolve, its carrier is the Symbol).
//   - lens/affected_set.dag (T-21) DERIVES the use→def graph by
//     `Symbol`-equality TRAVERSAL over the resolved tree (changed
//     declaration → its binder `Symbol` → every name-ref `Atom` with
//     that `Symbol` → enclosing declarations, transitively) — the same
//     "derive, don't store" discipline as `content_hash` (a fold) / D1.
//   - Binding MUST be NODE-PRECISE: a use-site's canonical `Symbol`
//     identifies the EXACT declaration, never merely its module/scope.
//     Coarse binding leaves affected_set correct but maximally
//     OVER-fires — node-precision is the dominant gate on R2
//     minimality. (Distinct axis from #3157's hash-granularity
//     "over-fire = safe": that is content identity; THIS is
//     dependency-edge granularity.) Authority: 03_resolve.dag B-4 note.
//
// T-9 (operator-ratified 2026-05-16) — the two contracts that make this
//   the keystone, single, decidable file:
//   A. FIND IS DECIDABLE BY CONSTRUCTION (closes C1). The
//      algebra-homomorphism Find recurses structurally on the Node tree
//      (A2 implicit descent — the same finite descent `node_well_formed`
//      uses, so the inferencer itself terminates). At each node the
//      candidate set is EXACTLY the CLOSED declared inhabitances
//      reachable in std/* — an enumerable set, never a synthesized or
//      open search space. So "no homomorphism" = "exhausted the finite
//      declared set" = a DECIDABLE fail-closed Diagnostic
//      (feedback_no_engine), not a search that may not terminate. A
//      T-9 worker *synthesizing* candidates (vs enumerating declared
//      inhabitances) has left the decidable fragment — STOP/escalate.
//   B. SINGLE-FILE DISCIPLINE IS A SCOPE BOUNDARY, not willpower (why
//      v2's 12-file split cannot recur). v2 split because env / scope /
//      lookup / method-resolution / signature concerns tangled. In v4
//      those are 03_resolve's job (B-4: binding = the canonical
//      `Symbol`, authored there). So 04_infer owns ONLY { the C1 Find
//      + cardinality propagation + diagnostic precision }. A T-9 worker
//      writing scope / env / binding / lookup / method-resolution here
//      has re-imported the 12-file pressure — that concern belongs in
//      03_resolve; STOP/escalate. The single file holds because the
//      scope is bounded, not because the file is willed small.
//
// Owns:
//   - InferredTree = Node + the frozen flat `InferredFacts` coordinate
//   - infer: ResolvedTree -> Result<InferredTree, Diagnostic>
//   - bounded algebra-homomorphism search (the U1 Find phase; C1)
//
// Consumes:
//   - std/node.dag, std/algebra.dag, std/cardinality.dag, std/diagnostic.dag
//   - compiler/03_resolve.dag: ResolvedTree
//
// Status: scaffold — fill per TASKS.md T-9


module v4.compiler.infer

